 A whisper drifts between the barrels...

 "Four shards of power -- runes -- lie scattered in this cellar.

  Some rest deep inside nested racks. One hides in the dark,
  behind the jars, where only a thorough search will reach it.

  A torch shows but one shelf. The 'find' spell sweeps them all.

  Sweep the cellar for every '.rune' shard and COUNT what you find:

  « find . -name '*.rune' | wc -l »

  The number of shards is the key that opens the cellar door.

  Beware: not everything down here is a rune. Wine notes and old
  ledgers will try to fool a careless count -- match only '*.rune'.

  One shard, the keystone, even bears its own name. Seek it by name:

  « find . -name 'keystone.rune' »

  When you know the number, work the « door » in this room."
